// CROWN crucible — the handler-residual face of the higher-order leak
// (Hβ.infer.handler-residual-outside-the-scheme): a handler-based HOF's
// residual must carry its CONFIG fn's row. run_each installs consume over
// the body; the arm calls f(x), so the residual is f's row — the install
// instantiates the handler's scheme, but a residual read off the raw decl
// handle bypasses that freshening and the callback's row never reaches
// run_each's published row. bad() then declares !E over a body that
// performs E through the config fn, and must REFUSE.
effect E { op() -> Int }
effect Feed { yield(x: Int) -> Int }
handler consume(f) {
  yield(x) => resume(f(x)),
}
fn run_each(f) = (yield(1)) ~> consume(f)
fn bad() with !E = run_each((x) => x + op())
fn main() = bad()
